# §506. What must never enter a build context.
#
# `apps/worker/Dockerfile` does `COPY apps/worker/ apps/worker/`, and there was
# no ignore file — so every image ever built carried `apps/worker/.env`, which
# `scripts/env-sync` writes with every credential this system holds. The
# container gets its environment from `docker run --env-file` and from
# Railway's own variables; the file has no business in a layer, where it
# survives in the image history whatever a later step deletes.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Weight, not secrecy: these make an upload slow and a build cache useless.
.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
.render-output
apps/web/public/dev-assets
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp
